Perfect — let’s build a structured roadmap of MySQL topics from Basic → Intermediate → Advanced, specifically framed for Data Engineering (DE) responsibilities. This way you’ll know exactly what to focus on at each stage.

🟢 Basic MySQL Topics (Foundation for DE)
These are the essentials every data engineer must master before moving into pipelines and warehouses.

Introduction to SQL & MySQL

What is SQL, RDBMS, NRDBMS

Database creation (CREATE DATABASE, USE)

Tables & Schema Basics

CREATE TABLE, ALTER TABLE, DROP TABLE

Rows, columns, datatypes (INT, VARCHAR, DATE, TIMESTAMP, DECIMAL, BLOB)

Constraints

PRIMARY KEY, FOREIGN KEY, UNIQUE, NOT NULL, DEFAULT, AUTO_INCREMENT

Basic Queries

SELECT, INSERT, UPDATE, DELETE

Filtering (WHERE, AND, OR, BETWEEN, IN)

Sorting (ORDER BY, LIMIT)

Aliases (AS), DISTINCT

Aggregations

COUNT, SUM, AVG, MIN, MAX

GROUP BY, HAVING

Joins (Intro)

INNER JOIN basics

Wildcards

LIKE, %, _

➡ DE Context: At this stage, you can design small schemas, clean raw data, and query staging tables.

🟡 Intermediate MySQL Topics (Pipeline & Analytics Focus)
Here you move beyond basics into more complex queries and schema design.

Advanced Joins

LEFT JOIN, RIGHT JOIN, FULL OUTER JOIN

UNION, INTERSECT

Subqueries & Nested Queries

Single-row, multi-row, correlated subqueries

Common Table Expressions (CTEs)

Simplify complex queries

Window Functions

ROW_NUMBER, RANK, DENSE_RANK, LEAD, LAG

Case Expressions

Conditional logic with CASE WHEN

Referential Actions

ON DELETE CASCADE vs ON DELETE SET NULL

Triggers

BEFORE/AFTER INSERT, UPDATE, DELETE

Views

Creating and using views for abstraction

Schema Design

ER diagrams, normalization (1NF, 2NF, 3NF)

➡ DE Context: You can now build ETL pipelines, deduplicate data, enforce business rules, and prepare datasets for analytics.

🔴 Advanced MySQL Topics (Data Engineering Mastery)
These are the skills that make you production-ready for large-scale systems.

Recursive CTEs

Hierarchical data (org charts, category trees)

Query Optimization

EXPLAIN plans, indexing strategies

Performance tuning for large datasets

Transactions & ACID

COMMIT, ROLLBACK, SAVEPOINT

Stored Procedures & Functions

Automating logic inside the database

Partitioning & Sharding

Handling big data across multiple servers

Materialized Views

Precomputed query results for performance

Data Warehousing Concepts

Star schema, snowflake schema

Fact and dimension tables

Integration with Cloud DE Tools

MySQL with BigQuery, Snowflake, Redshift

Security & User Management

GRANT, REVOKE, roles, permissions

➡ DE Context: At this level, you’re designing enterprise-scale data warehouses, optimizing queries for millions of rows, and integrating SQL with cloud platforms and pipelines.

✅ Summary
Basic: Schema design, CRUD operations, simple joins, aggregates.

Intermediate: Complex joins, CTEs, window functions, triggers, ER diagrams.

Advanced: Optimization, transactions, recursive queries, warehouse schemas, cloud integration.
